WEBVTT

00:12.012 --> 00:13.596
BALLAD OF THE HAPPY DESTRUCTION

00:19.978 --> 00:25.817
We can finally start handing out food
to the newcomers as well.

00:25.900 --> 00:27.986
No need to produce and sell Back Powder.

00:28.069 --> 00:31.948
The wealth in this mansion is plenty
to provide for us.

00:32.032 --> 00:34.659
The boss still hasn't come back yet.

00:34.743 --> 00:37.370
It seems Ton and Natsuki have come back.

00:37.454 --> 00:41.207
Apparently, they want to gather everyone
and show them something.

00:50.550 --> 00:52.886
Amazing! There isn't a single scratch!

00:52.969 --> 00:55.263
A defensive type of magic.

00:55.346 --> 00:57.849
We failed to capture Kikurage,

00:57.932 --> 01:01.770
but Natsuki's magic awakened
during the fight with the En family!

01:02.353 --> 01:07.067
This thing that looks like
a protective suit might even repel magic.

01:07.150 --> 01:09.277
Yeah! Let's try it next time!

01:09.360 --> 01:13.531
But if Natsuki can use magic this amazing,

01:13.615 --> 01:16.284
she doesn't need to be in the Cross-Eyes.

01:16.910 --> 01:19.746
She can make a good living
with this magic.

01:19.829 --> 01:22.749
Now that you mention it, you're right.

01:28.671 --> 01:30.381
Hey, your left eye...

01:30.465 --> 01:33.635
After we returned to the mansion
and healed my arm,

01:34.135 --> 01:36.638
I had a cross tattooed on this eye too!

01:38.556 --> 01:39.891
Everyone,

01:39.974 --> 01:44.395
even now that I can use magic,
I'll always be part of the Cross-Eyes!

01:46.356 --> 01:47.482
Natsuki...

01:47.982 --> 01:51.319
Or that's just how I personally feel.

01:51.402 --> 01:53.988
Can I stay here?

01:54.072 --> 01:56.157
Of course you can!

01:56.241 --> 01:59.744
If we get into trouble,
you'll protect us with that magic.

01:59.828 --> 02:01.496
Everyone...

02:03.081 --> 02:06.709
You're officially a member
of the Cross-Eyes from today.

02:06.793 --> 02:08.002
Saji...

02:09.003 --> 02:12.090
Everyone. Thank you!

03:40.887 --> 03:42.931
THE BEGINNING

03:47.518 --> 03:52.690
I never thought I'd turn into a man
and come back here again.

03:52.774 --> 03:56.069
You've become quite handsome, Nikaido.

03:57.737 --> 04:00.406
You're a completely different person now.

04:01.908 --> 04:05.286
By the way,
these clothes are really heavy.

04:05.787 --> 04:10.291
They've been made heavy with magic
because your training is still ongoing.

04:10.792 --> 04:14.921
Also, the magic that changes your sex
only lasts for four hours.

04:15.505 --> 04:19.676
After that, you'll return
to your original form, so be careful.

04:20.843 --> 04:23.179
Got it. Four hours.

04:23.972 --> 04:25.431
So, around nine o'clock.

04:28.935 --> 04:31.938
I once heard this from a fellow Devil.

04:32.730 --> 04:36.025
Apparently, there's a room
somewhere in this mansion

04:36.109 --> 04:39.570
that stores only the valuables
En got as gifts from Devils.

04:39.654 --> 04:41.531
Does anything come to mind?

04:43.616 --> 04:45.159
Come to think of it,

04:45.243 --> 04:50.498
En once took me to a strange room
and made me listen to endless bragging.

04:50.581 --> 04:52.458
Maybe it's the room from then.

04:52.542 --> 04:54.002
If I remember right,

04:54.085 --> 04:57.839
some kind of object
served as a hidden door.

04:59.340 --> 05:01.092
Let's try looking for it.

05:05.013 --> 05:08.516
Is this room also used
by an En family officer?

05:08.599 --> 05:10.601
Yeah, it's Noi's room.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.770
All right, let's grab the valuables.

05:12.854 --> 05:14.605
We're good with cash already.

05:14.689 --> 05:16.941
We're after a clue

05:17.025 --> 05:20.486
to where the remaining En family members
might be hiding, right?

05:20.987 --> 05:23.740
There are a lot of photos.

05:24.949 --> 05:28.953
When the boss comes back,
let's all take a photo together too!

05:29.037 --> 05:29.871
Yes!

05:30.580 --> 05:32.623
I'm looking forward to it.

05:39.213 --> 05:43.009
Hey, it's been a while,
all you Cross-Eyes' officers.

05:43.968 --> 05:45.386
Risu?!

05:45.470 --> 05:49.932
Thanks to this cross mark,
which I'm thinking of erasing now,

05:50.016 --> 05:51.893
I was able to get in easily.

05:51.976 --> 05:55.438
There's something I want to ask you guys.

05:55.938 --> 06:00.902
Risu, like I said before,
we don't know who killed you.

06:02.904 --> 06:08.159
Then maybe Dokuga
is hiding something from you guys.

06:09.702 --> 06:13.289
He seemed to know a lot about me.

06:14.499 --> 06:18.753
All right.
I'll have Dokuga tell me directly.

06:19.587 --> 06:21.756
We won't let you go to Dokuga!

06:21.839 --> 06:25.009
Then try to stop me, you scumbags!

06:31.099 --> 06:33.851
I feel it. I can feel it.

06:33.935 --> 06:35.937
Your murderous intent!

06:42.902 --> 06:46.322
Just as I thought,
there were no guards at this entrance.

06:48.616 --> 06:51.953
I'm glad I worked part-time for Mr. Tanba.

06:52.995 --> 06:55.206
Anyway, I have to find Risu.

07:04.298 --> 07:07.593
Dokuga, what are you going to do
about Natsuki?

07:08.177 --> 07:11.681
She might get killed, just like Risu.

07:12.723 --> 07:16.394
Natsuki might get killed?
What are they talking about?

07:18.479 --> 07:21.774
If the boss sets his eyes
on Natsuki's magic...

07:21.858 --> 07:23.901
Natsuki's magic?

07:23.985 --> 07:26.946
You're not just gonna
stand by and watch, are you?

07:27.029 --> 07:29.657
I'm against it! We need to find some way--

07:29.740 --> 07:32.285
I'm thinking of giving Natsuki
some mission

07:32.368 --> 07:34.203
to keep her away from here.

07:35.037 --> 07:37.707
During that time, I'll talk to the boss.

07:41.043 --> 07:44.213
I'll tell him not to kill
any more of our comrades.

07:46.632 --> 07:47.717
I...

07:49.469 --> 07:53.723
I, once again,
want to try believing in the boss.

07:55.183 --> 07:56.476
Dokuga.

08:00.563 --> 08:05.109
Because the boss is the one
who gave us a reason to live.

08:06.402 --> 08:11.532
To us worthless ones who can't use magic,
he gave a path other than just dying.

08:14.118 --> 08:16.704
Yeah. You're right, Dokuga.

08:17.413 --> 08:18.748
Let's believe in the boss.

08:20.041 --> 08:21.584
I'm sure he'll understand.

08:28.716 --> 08:31.594
This area is En's private space.

08:31.677 --> 08:34.680
There were things
like bedrooms for me and Kikurage.

08:34.764 --> 08:36.015
I see.

08:36.098 --> 08:38.893
Maybe it's somewhere near here.

08:38.976 --> 08:40.853
Who are they?

08:40.937 --> 08:43.189
Only officers are allowed in here.

08:43.272 --> 08:44.649
Leave it to me.

08:46.067 --> 08:48.152
I think I might remember something.

08:48.236 --> 08:49.654
You guys!

08:49.737 --> 08:51.155
Show me your arms!

08:51.239 --> 08:52.907
I'll check your smoke.

08:53.491 --> 08:56.536
Looks like some troublemakers found us.

08:56.619 --> 08:59.914
They're probably Cross-Eyes officers.
What do we do, Asu?

08:59.997 --> 09:02.416
Come on, hurry up and show me your arms!

09:02.500 --> 09:05.461
This is part of your training too.
Deal with him.

09:05.545 --> 09:07.672
I'll look for the book.

09:07.755 --> 09:09.048
She disappeared...

09:16.597 --> 09:17.723
Take that!

09:21.227 --> 09:23.271
My clothes are heavy!

09:26.315 --> 09:27.733
Got you!

09:47.712 --> 09:49.505
Sorry, Dokuga.

09:49.589 --> 09:52.425
Tetsujo, you let your guard down.

09:53.384 --> 09:54.260
And you...

09:55.219 --> 09:56.345
Who are you?

09:57.388 --> 10:00.516
Why are Cross-Eyes fighting each other?

10:05.855 --> 10:07.106
He's fast!

10:09.108 --> 10:11.777
If I keep wearing this, I'll get killed.

10:33.716 --> 10:34.717
Dokuga!

10:42.475 --> 10:45.394
Damn it! You bastard!

10:45.478 --> 10:47.521
- You're getting--
- Too cocky!

10:55.237 --> 10:58.074
I'm not dealing with you all day. Now!

11:00.576 --> 11:02.370
Ouch.

11:02.870 --> 11:04.038
What? You?

11:04.121 --> 11:05.748
That hurts...

11:17.093 --> 11:19.762
What on earth have you been looking at?

11:20.471 --> 11:22.848
It's Caiman's medical record.

11:22.932 --> 11:28.020
Looking at this,
it's clear that Caiman is human.

11:28.104 --> 11:32.024
But I checked the records,
and something's been bothering me.

11:33.067 --> 11:35.528
Since Caiman is a victim of magic,

11:35.611 --> 11:38.531
isn't it only natural
that something's abnormal?

11:38.614 --> 11:41.325
That's not what I mean.

11:41.409 --> 11:43.160
Well, how should I put it?

11:45.121 --> 11:49.542
I wish I could talk this over
with Mr. Kasukabe.

11:49.625 --> 11:55.673
Maybe this is the reason
why Caiman's head regenerates.

11:57.550 --> 12:01.178
But it's already been a month since then.

12:02.221 --> 12:07.101
I wonder what happened
to Caiman and Nikaido.

12:07.935 --> 12:13.357
QUESTION & ANSWER

12:15.776 --> 12:18.112
He should've escaped this way.

12:18.195 --> 12:21.073
Damn it. Looks like we lost him.

12:21.157 --> 12:22.950
This is why big houses are...

12:23.033 --> 12:25.619
More importantly,
Dokuga, is your head okay?

12:26.370 --> 12:27.705
Yeah...

12:28.205 --> 12:31.292
I bet he went through the passageway.
Let's go!

12:34.795 --> 12:37.840
All right, looks like we managed
to shake them off.

12:37.923 --> 12:39.592
What the hell are you?

12:39.675 --> 12:43.137
Why do I have to hide
together with a Cross-Eyes?

12:44.764 --> 12:48.100
Come on, you know it's bad for you
to be here too.

12:48.934 --> 12:50.978
That's it! I remember now.

12:51.061 --> 12:52.354
It's this stone statue.

12:52.938 --> 12:55.316
En really thought this through.

12:55.399 --> 12:58.360
If it's a Devil statue,
no one would touch it.

12:59.236 --> 13:00.821
If I remember correctly...

13:02.072 --> 13:05.367
Is it okay to do something like that
to a Devil statue?

13:09.455 --> 13:10.498
Oh my.

13:10.581 --> 13:13.876
Found it!
It's the entrance to En's treasure room.

13:13.959 --> 13:15.711
You get in too.

13:15.795 --> 13:17.630
Hide until things cool down.

13:17.713 --> 13:19.590
What? Why me?

13:19.673 --> 13:21.675
- I'm busy, so...
- Just get in!

13:29.141 --> 13:31.894
What is this room?

13:31.977 --> 13:36.941
This is a room filled only
with the treasure En really cherished.

13:37.024 --> 13:39.068
Treasure?

13:39.151 --> 13:41.362
It looks like a bunch of junk to me.

13:41.445 --> 13:45.407
And who the hell are you?
You've been acting like you know me.

13:45.491 --> 13:48.744
What, you still haven't figured it out?

13:48.828 --> 13:49.787
It's me.

13:49.870 --> 13:51.497
Nikaido.

13:51.580 --> 13:55.042
I disguised myself as a man using magic
to sneak in here.

13:55.125 --> 13:56.669
What?

13:56.752 --> 13:59.171
You're Nikaido?

13:59.755 --> 14:02.424
Now that you mention it...

14:02.508 --> 14:05.052
- Quit lying, you asshole!
- Ouch!

14:06.679 --> 14:08.848
You're hurt!

14:08.931 --> 14:11.725
Don't worry. It's nothing serious.

14:11.809 --> 14:14.728
- All right, I've got to find the book.
- What?

14:16.063 --> 14:18.524
Man, I'm hungry.

14:19.358 --> 14:22.444
Oh, right.
I'll eat the curry bread that I brought.

14:22.528 --> 14:24.446
TO EN, CHIDARUMA
A LUCKY DAY IN MARCH

14:24.530 --> 14:29.118
I mean, even if you say Nikaido,
we only just met the other day.

14:29.201 --> 14:31.954
I don't even remember your face.

14:34.039 --> 14:36.333
There it is. It has to be this book!

14:36.834 --> 14:37.960
What's that?

14:38.043 --> 14:40.796
You came all the way here
just to steal that book?

14:41.297 --> 14:42.214
Yeah.

14:42.298 --> 14:46.343
This book contains
the information I need to use my magic.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.974
Oh crap! It's already nine o'clock!

15:07.656 --> 15:10.409
See. I told you it was true.

15:14.747 --> 15:16.457
Nikaido...

15:18.125 --> 15:19.460
Caiman...

15:20.753 --> 15:26.967
I told you,
I'm not that guy called Caiman!

15:27.051 --> 15:27.927
Give it a rest!

15:28.010 --> 15:32.348
That's true, I did name you Caiman
without much thought.

15:33.015 --> 15:39.229
But when you turned back, are you saying
you forgot about me, the Hole, and gyoza?

15:39.772 --> 15:41.398
Gyoza...

15:41.899 --> 15:44.693
Stop it!
I don't know anything about gyoza!

15:45.527 --> 15:49.156
I heard officers are fighting a monster!
Let's go take a look!

15:49.865 --> 15:50.991
What's going on?

15:53.869 --> 15:55.412
You guys, back off!

15:55.496 --> 15:57.539
It's dangerous! Back off!

15:57.623 --> 15:59.166
Damn it. How pathetic.

15:59.750 --> 16:02.336
We can't attack Curse from our side.

16:02.419 --> 16:05.172
We need to think of a way
to chase him away.

16:05.798 --> 16:08.968
- We have to make him talk to Dokuga.
- Please wait!

16:09.927 --> 16:11.971
I'll use my magic to deal with him!

16:12.054 --> 16:13.931
Please, everyone, stay back!

16:14.014 --> 16:14.848
Natsuki!

16:15.933 --> 16:17.810
Isn't that Natsuki?

16:18.769 --> 16:21.605
What's that black thing over there?

16:22.690 --> 16:28.529
That's reckless, Natsuki.
He's a relentless, cursed bastard. Hey!

16:28.612 --> 16:32.741
I'm surprised. She was able to use magic.

16:43.168 --> 16:46.046
If it comes down to it,
we'll all help Natsuki.

16:47.131 --> 16:50.050
I feel it. I can feel it.

16:50.134 --> 16:51.802
Your murderous intent!

17:05.315 --> 17:06.483
Risu!

17:26.128 --> 17:28.172
- Nikaido.
- Asu.

17:28.255 --> 17:29.506
So you were here.

17:29.590 --> 17:31.091
I've caught him!

17:31.175 --> 17:32.760
Good job, Natsuki!

17:32.843 --> 17:33.886
You're amazing!

17:33.969 --> 17:35.262
What should we do?

17:35.345 --> 17:37.014
Hang him outside the window!

17:41.060 --> 17:41.935
Hey!

17:42.019 --> 17:42.895
That guy...

17:43.645 --> 17:46.106
What's wrong? What's all this commotion?

17:46.190 --> 17:47.316
Dokuga!

17:47.399 --> 17:49.985
Risu turned into Curse and attacked us.

17:50.069 --> 17:50.903
What?

17:50.986 --> 17:54.698
But Natsuki beat him with magic.

17:54.782 --> 17:58.577
We found out that Natsuki's magic
can fight against curses too.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.540
Natsuki, come with us.

18:07.711 --> 18:08.545
Risu.

18:08.629 --> 18:10.130
Hey, Risu!

18:17.137 --> 18:21.058
- Risu! Wake up!
- So that monster from earlier was Risu?

18:21.642 --> 18:25.229
Nikaido, we've got the book.
Let's get out of here soon.

18:25.312 --> 18:26.313
Yeah, right.

18:27.106 --> 18:28.816
Hey, you're...

18:28.899 --> 18:31.318
Kawajiri. It's been a while, Aikawa.

18:32.402 --> 18:35.739
Aikawa. Let's get out of here together.

18:36.907 --> 18:41.245
I can't go with you guys.

18:43.288 --> 18:45.165
But take care of him.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.584
He's my partner.

18:47.668 --> 18:51.505
Risu is your partner?
So that's how it was.

18:52.047 --> 18:55.592
Got it. Leave it to me.
But what are you going to do?

18:55.676 --> 19:00.347
And you've been avoiding me
from the start. Why is that?

19:00.430 --> 19:03.225
Even if you remember, just like before...

19:06.061 --> 19:07.688
What's wrong? Are you okay?

19:07.771 --> 19:09.481
Don't come near me!

19:10.649 --> 19:12.276
Don't come near me!

19:13.652 --> 19:17.489
You surely have your own life,
so it can't be helped.

19:18.073 --> 19:20.200
But come eat some gyoza again.

19:20.951 --> 19:22.744
I'll give you a 20% discount.

19:24.246 --> 19:26.331
I can't anymore...

19:26.957 --> 19:28.250
I...

19:30.085 --> 19:31.753
Nikaido, let's go already!

19:33.046 --> 19:34.339
Caiman...

19:46.059 --> 19:47.019
I'm sick of it.

19:48.604 --> 19:50.022
My head!

19:50.856 --> 19:52.524
I'm sick of it!

20:07.122 --> 20:08.790
I'm sick of it...

20:12.920 --> 20:14.546
Why do you refuse?

20:18.383 --> 20:19.551
Shut up...

20:19.635 --> 20:22.054
You, from the very start...

20:30.854 --> 20:32.439
never existed.

21:40.173 --> 21:43.218
Yay! A mission!

21:43.302 --> 21:47.806
I can't believe Dokuga is
letting me do a job all by myself.

21:50.976 --> 21:53.478
So it's a search for an elite Sorcerer.

21:54.646 --> 21:56.982
It's pretty far away.

21:57.065 --> 22:01.528
At least, I wanted the boss
to see my magic.

22:03.322 --> 22:06.992
But he said to keep a low profile
and leave through the back door.

22:07.075 --> 22:08.827
I wonder why?

22:13.081 --> 22:14.499
Boss!

22:15.292 --> 22:17.377
Excuse me!

22:20.297 --> 22:23.717
I'm about to head out on a mission.

22:23.800 --> 22:26.470
So, well...

22:26.553 --> 22:30.474
When I get back, can we Cross-Eyes
all take a picture together?

22:34.061 --> 22:36.229
I want you.

22:36.313 --> 22:37.689
Boss...

22:52.871 --> 22:54.998
Boss...

22:55.832 --> 22:57.709
Why...

24:53.658 --> 24:54.951
THE END

24:55.035 --> 24:57.162
What we learned in Episode 11.

24:57.245 --> 24:59.247
There's a clue in Caiman's medical file.

24:59.331 --> 25:01.166
Aikawa entrusted Risu to Nikaido.

25:01.249 --> 25:03.919
Natsuki wanted
to take a picture with everyone.

25:04.002 --> 25:07.964
What we'll learn in Season 3
is still hidden in chaos.

25:08.048 --> 25:09.883
This is Dorohedoro.
